<title>USA: Centennial class-action suits expanded.</title>
<headline>Centennial class-action suits expanded.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The law firm of Savett Frutkin Podell &amp; Ryan PC said on Thursday that the U.S. District Court for Massachusetts has extended the class period for shareholder class actions regarding Centennial Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>The suits now include investors who bought Centennial stock between April 12, 1994 and February 25, 1997.</p>
<p>The suits allege that Centennial and two of its senior officers issued false and misleading financial statements.</p>
<p>Emanuel Pinez, Centennial's former chief executive, was indicted this week on five charges of securities fraud. If convicted he faces up to 10 years in prison and a fine of $1 million per count.</p>
